+# Secrets defined here are available for reference under registry/password, env/secret, builder/secrets,
+# and accessories/*/env/secret in config/deploy.yml. All secrets should be pulled from either a
+# password manager, ENV, or a file. DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE! This file needs to be safe for git.
+
+# Generate with `bin/rails secret`.
+SECRET_KEY_BASE=$SECRET_KEY_BASE
+
+# SMTP password / API key for your mail server (leave unset if your mail server does not require auth).
+SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD
+
+# Optional: Uncomment to enable browser Web Push notifications.
+# Generate keys with:
+#   bin/rails runner 'k = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{k.public_key}\nVAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{k.private_key}"'
+# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=$VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
+# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=$VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY
+
+# Optional: Needed only if you switch from the local registry to an external authenticated registry.
+# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
+
+# Alternative: Fetch secrets from a password manager (1Password, Bitwarden, LastPass, etc.)
+# SECRETS=$(kamal secrets fetch --adapter 1password --account your-account --from Vault/Fizzy SECRET_KEY_BASE SMTP_PASSWORD)
+# SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(kamal secrets extract SECRET_KEY_BASE ${SECRETS})
+# SMTP_PASSWORD=$(kamal secrets extract SMTP_PASSWORD ${SECRETS})
